<overview>
<p>Foot infantry platoons are the most basic and numerous conventional military formation across the Inner Sphere and Periphery. Deployed on foot without dedicated transport, these platoons are slow to reposition but cheap to raise, easy to supply, and capable of holding ground that faster units cannot afford to garrison permanently. Every major military fields foot platoons in enormous numbers for planetary defense, installation security, and rear-area policing. Their lack of mobility makes them poorly suited for offensive operations against armored forces, but in prepared defensive positions, urban terrain, or dense forests, dismounted infantry remain difficult to dislodge without committing disproportionate resources.</p><p>Heavy weapons teams carry recoilless rifles that provide a portable anti-armor capability, allowing infantry to engage vehicles and hardened positions that would otherwise require dedicated support weapons. Eventually retired in favor of infantry-scale SRMs these weapons later experienced a resurgence as budgets and access to complex manufacturing were threatened.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as generic early date, prior to most advanced infantry equipment
